IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tda-common`

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Tas) ss 3-6 -- the terms both Acts use: home, new home, established home, relevant
-- interest, owner, spouse, residential property. Encoded once, here, and used by the Duties Act modules and the grant
-- module alike.
--
-- Duties Act 2001 s 3 "home": "(b) for the purposes of Divisions 2A and 2B of Part 5 of Chapter 2, and Division 2 of
-- Part 6 of Chapter 2, has the same meaning as in the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000"; ss 46A and 57C give "new home"
-- and "owner" the same meaning as in that Act, and "established home means a home other than a new home"; s 46J gives
-- "owner" that meaning for Division 2B. The Duties Act keeps its own "spouse" (s 3), which this module also states,
-- because it differs (finding 9).
--
-- Source: ../../../first-home-owner-grant-act-2000/registers/source-bundle/act-2000-019.txt (consolidation published
-- 2026-10-14) and ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2001-015.txt. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation
-- website at 20 October 2026 (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 ss 3-6 -- the shared terms`

§§ `s 4 home; s 3 new home; Duties Act ss 46A, 57C established home`

-- s 4: "A home is a building (affixed to land) that -- (a) may lawfully be used as a place of residence; and (b) is, in
-- the Commissioner's opinion, a suitable building for use as a place of residence."
-- s 3 "new home means -- (a) a home that has not previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence; or (b) a
-- home that -- (i) under section 40-75(1)(b) of the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 of the
-- Commonwealth, would be considered new residential premises due to substantial renovations; and (ii) has not been
-- occupied or sold as a place of residence since those substantial renovations were completed".
-- The GST Act test is a borrowed term: a FACT. The Commissioner's opinion is answered conditionally: a FACT.
DECLARE `Building facts` HAS
    `is a building affixed to land`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `may lawfully be used as a place of residence`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `is, in the Commissioner's opinion, suitable for use as a place of residence`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `would be new residential premises because of substantial renovations (GST Act s 40-75(1)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since those renovations`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `b` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a home (FHOG Act s 4)` IF
        `b`'s `is a building affixed to land`
    AND `b`'s `may lawfully be used as a place of residence`
    AND `b`'s `is, in the Commissioner's opinion, suitable for use as a place of residence`

GIVEN `b` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a new home (FHOG Act s 3)` IF
        `is a home (FHOG Act s 4)` `b`
    AND (    (NOT `b`'s `has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence`)
         OR (    `b`'s `would be new residential premises because of substantial renovations (GST Act s 40-75(1)(b))`
             AND (NOT `b`'s `has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since those renovations`)))

-- Duties Act ss 46A, 57C: "established home means a home other than a new home".
GIVEN `b` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an established home (Duties Act ss 46A, 57C)` IF
        `is a home (FHOG Act s 4)` `b`
    AND (NOT `is a new home (FHOG Act s 3)` `b`)

-- What kind of home a building is, for a buyer choosing between the duty exemption and the grant.
DECLARE `Kind of home` IS ONE OF
    `not a home (FHOG Act s 4)`
    `a new home (FHOG Act s 3)`
    `an established home (Duties Act ss 46A, 57C)`

GIVEN `b` IS A `Building facts`
GIVETH A `Kind of home`
`the kind of home` MEANS
    IF (NOT `is a home (FHOG Act s 4)` `b`)
    THEN `not a home (FHOG Act s 4)`
    ELSE IF `is a new home (FHOG Act s 3)` `b`
         THEN `a new home (FHOG Act s 3)`
         ELSE `an established home (Duties Act ss 46A, 57C)`

§§ `s 5 relevant interest and owner`

-- s 5(2): "Each of the following is, subject to subsection (2A) and (3), a relevant interest in land: (a) an estate in
-- fee simple in the land; (b) a life estate in the land approved by the Commissioner; (c) a perpetual lease of the land
-- granted by the Commonwealth or the State; (d) a leasehold interest in the land granted by the Commonwealth or the State
-- that may be converted ... into an estate in fee simple; (e) an interest as purchaser under a contract for the purchase
-- from the Commonwealth or the State of an estate in fee simple in the land by instalments; (f) a licence or right of
-- occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State that gives, in the Commissioner's opinion, ... reasonable security
-- of tenure; (g) an interest in a company's shares if the Commissioner is satisfied that -- (i) the interest entitles the
-- holder ... to exclusive occupation of a specified home owned by the company; and (ii) the value of the shares is not
-- less than the value of the company's interest in the home."
-- (2A): "Any interest in land held by, or to be held by, the Commonwealth, or Housing Australia, as a result of a Help to
-- Buy arrangement is not a relevant interest in land."
-- (3): "(a) an interest is not a relevant interest at a particular time unless the holder ... has, or will have within
-- 12 months after that time (or a longer time allowed by the Commissioner), a right to immediate occupation of the land;
-- and (b) an interest is not a relevant interest in the hands of a person who holds it subject to a trust; and (c) an
-- equitable interest is not a relevant interest unless it is the interest of a person under a legal disability for whom
-- a guardian holds the interest on trust."
-- (4): the Commissioner "may recognise an interest (a non-conforming interest) as a relevant interest ... even though
-- the interest may not conform with subsections (2) and (3)". READING: (4) names (2) and (3), not (2A), so a Help to
-- Buy interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia cannot be recognised.
DECLARE `Kind of interest` IS ONE OF
    `an estate in fee simple`
    `a life estate`
    `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State`
    `a leasehold granted by the Commonwealth or the State that may be converted to fee simple`
    `a purchaser's interest in an instalment purchase of fee simple from the Commonwealth or the State`
    `a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State`
    `an interest in company shares giving exclusive occupation of a home the company owns`
    `an interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement`
    `another interest`

DECLARE `Interest facts` HAS
    `kind`                                                                         IS A `Kind of interest`
    -- (b) approved; (f) in the Commissioner's opinion reasonably secure; (g) the Commissioner satisfied of (i) and (ii).
    `the Commissioner approves it, or is of the opinion or satisfied that s 5(2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives a right to immediate occupation now or within 12 months (or a longer time allowed)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is held subject to a trust`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an equitable interest`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is held on trust by a guardian for a person under a legal disability`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner recognises it as a non-conforming interest (s 5(4))`         IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `i` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is listed in s 5(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `i`'s `kind`
    WHEN `an estate in fee simple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a life estate` THEN `i`'s `the Commissioner approves it, or is of the opinion or satisfied that s 5(2) requires`
    WHEN `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a leasehold granted by the Commonwealth or the State that may be converted to fee simple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a purchaser's interest in an instalment purchase of fee simple from the Commonwealth or the State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State` THEN `i`'s `the Commissioner approves it, or is of the opinion or satisfied that s 5(2) requires`
    WHEN `an interest in company shares giving exclusive occupation of a home the company owns` THEN `i`'s `the Commissioner approves it, or is of the opinion or satisfied that s 5(2) requires`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `i` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Help to Buy interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia (s 5(2A))` IF
    CONSIDER `i`'s `kind`
    WHEN `an interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `i` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a relevant interest in land (FHOG Act s 5(2)-(4))` IF
        (NOT `is a Help to Buy interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia (s 5(2A))` `i`)
    AND (    `i`'s `the Commissioner recognises it as a non-conforming interest (s 5(4))`
         OR (    `the kind is listed in s 5(2)` `i`
             AND `i`'s `gives a right to immediate occupation now or within 12 months (or a longer time allowed)`
             AND (NOT `i`'s `is held subject to a trust`)
             AND (    (NOT `i`'s `is an equitable interest`)
                  OR `i`'s `is held on trust by a guardian for a person under a legal disability`)))

-- s 5(1): "A person is an owner of a home or a home owner if the person has a relevant interest in land on which a home
-- is built." s 3 "owner means -- (a) in relation to land, a person who has a relevant interest in the land; and (b) in
-- relation to a home, a person who has a relevant interest in the land on which the home is built".
GIVEN `i` IS AN `Interest facts`
      `the building on the land` IS A `Building facts`
      `a building is on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `makes the holder an owner of a home (FHOG Act ss 3, 5(1))` IF
        `is a relevant interest in land (FHOG Act s 5(2)-(4))` `i`
    AND `a building is on the land`
    AND `is a home (FHOG Act s 4)` `the building on the land`

§§ `s 6 spouse (FHOG Act); s 3 spouse (Duties Act)`

-- FHOG Act s 6(1): "A person is the spouse of another if -- (a) they are legally married; or (b) they are in a
-- significant relationship, within the meaning of the Relationships Act 2003." (2): "If the Commissioner is satisfied
-- that, at the time of deciding an application ... an applicant -- (a) is legally married but not cohabiting with the
-- person to whom the applicant is legally married; and (b) has no intention of resuming cohabitation -- the person to
-- whom the applicant is legally married is not to be regarded as the applicant's spouse."
-- Duties Act s 3: "spouse, in relation to a person, includes the person who is in a significant relationship with that
-- person"; it has no rule like s 6(2). "Significant relationship" is a borrowed term (Relationships Act 2003): a FACT.
DECLARE `Relationship facts` HAS
    `are legally married`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `are in a significant relationship (Relationships Act 2003)`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `are not cohabiting, with no intention of resuming cohabitation`               IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `r` IS A `Relationship facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a spouse for the grant (FHOG Act s 6)` IF
        (    `r`'s `are legally married`
         AND (NOT `r`'s `are not cohabiting, with no intention of resuming cohabitation`))
    OR `r`'s `are in a significant relationship (Relationships Act 2003)`

GIVEN `r` IS A `Relationship facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a spouse for the Duties Act (s 3)` IF
        `r`'s `are legally married`
    OR `r`'s `are in a significant relationship (Relationships Act 2003)`

§§ `s 3(2) residential property`

-- s 3(2): "land in Australia is residential property at a particular time if there is, at that time, a building on the
-- land lawfully occupied as a place of residence and suitable for occupation as a place of residence."
GIVEN `in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a building on it is lawfully occupied as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that building is suitable for occupation as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is residential property (FHOG Act s 3(2))` IF
        `in Australia`
    AND `a building on it is lawfully occupied as a place of residence`
    AND `that building is suitable for occupation as a place of residence`
